{"classification":"mathematical-missing-union-scope","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0088","math_ordinal":37,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH21-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"To prove the symmetric difference for the union is countable, the right side must be the union of the countable symmetric differences.  Parentheses make the intended scope of the union explicit.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt216.tex:129-130","source_normalized_sha256":"6a391fcf933046f39da6a342c6b26714e50edfab95d6f6e4d27354a8397621c7","source_text":"$E[\\{0\\}]\\symmdiff E[\\{1\\}]\\subseteq\\bigcup_{n\\in\\Bbb N}E_n[\\{0\\}]\\symmdiff E_n[\\{1\\}]$","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt216.tex:127-128","target_normalized_sha256":"0c9d9ee0694c9cd0a33db7c2933e9a1a44059b19dc45f788cbc6e80769c14c83","target_text":"$E[\\{0\\}]\\symmdiff E[\\{1\\}]\\subseteq\\bigcup_{n\\in\\Bbb N}(E_n[\\{0\\}]\\symmdiff E_n[\\{1\\}])$","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S216"}
{"classification":"mathematical-type-error","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0089","math_ordinal":299,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH21-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"E is a measurable subset of X and therefore an element of the sigma-algebra Sigma, not a subset of that family.  The following sentence also uses E in every Sigma_gamma.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt216.tex:422-423","source_normalized_sha256":"ed6a4766660afffd90ee02908bf36f7b838e7834b2e654cb2d7cf5e7ea696049","source_text":"$A\\subseteq E\\subseteq\\Sigma$","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt216.tex:436-437","target_normalized_sha256":"9843fd581b22f8651080272188e36a7afa47e1ace788269143ec301c69a0b5bb","target_text":"$A\\subseteq E\\in\\Sigma$","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S216"}
{"classification":"mathematical-wrong-ambient-and-duplicate-index","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0090","math_ordinal":362,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH21-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The function x belongs to {0,1}^I, so its remaining coordinates range over I rather than the index set C.  The two prescribed pieces are K_j and K_k; repeating K_j leaves the K_k branch inconsistent with the intended piecewise definition.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt216.tex:484-486","source_normalized_sha256":"6473c507490fe536b4ff9b66d57b9455eb13c91f65edac26f2e72f41f8f39e7b","source_text":"$C\\setminus(K_j\\cup K_j)$","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt216.tex:503-505","target_normalized_sha256":"677fce5a77f706e2a94b04028c78a307cb727b30c7db64dc708b94f215472fbb","target_text":"$I\\setminus(K_j\\cup K_k)$","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S216"}
